    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 19,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "vg-media-processor is a **pure-Go** service (STT/TTS streaming + VAD gate) \u2014 unlike silero it does **not** use CGo/ONNX, so RSS should track the Go heap closely. Read the split: **`heap_inuse` climbing \u2192 Go-side leak** (goroutines, unbounded maps/slices, audio ring buffers); take a pprof heap diff. **RSS climbing while `heap_sys` stays flat** \u2192 off-heap growth (mmap'd buffers, cgo in a vendor SDK) \u2014 the *Estimated off-heap* panel surfaces it. **`goroutines` climbing \u2192 goroutine leak** (e.g. per-session STT/TTS readers or websocket pumps not exiting). Requires the media-processor PodMonitor + `podMonitors.enabled` (already on in voicegateway-dev)."
      }
    },
